# =============================================================================
# state.manifest — what `scripts/fks-state.sh export` bundles into an encrypted
# snapshot. Copy to `state.manifest` (gitignored) and tune to your deployment.
#
# Lines are either:
#   • a file or glob, relative to the repo root — optionally prefixed `file:`
#     (e.g. .env, models/*.bin). Sibling-repo paths (`../fks-state/...`) work:
#     the snapshot is anchored at the PARENT directory of this checkout, so
#     `..` paths round-trip through export/import.
#   • db:<database>[:table1,table2,...]           dumped via the postgres container
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Missing file matches are skipped with
# a warning, so it's safe to list paths you don't always have.
#
# NOTHING here should ever be committed to the public repo — this manifest only
# names the private surface; the snapshot itself lives in the private fks-state
# repo, age-encrypted.
# =============================================================================

# ── Secrets & TLS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.secrets
infrastructure/certs/

# ── Strategy configs — the edge (the sibling bot repos' tuned params) ────────
# These live in the sibling checkouts (the `crypto` repo is dissolved: the spot
# bot lives in fks-spawner, the futures/funding edges in the private
# fks-state). Point at them directly — `../` paths are supported. Uncomment
# what applies:
# ../fks-state/bots/crypto-futures/funding.toml
# ../fks-spawner/bots/spot-portfolio/spot-portfolio.toml

# ── Model weights / optimizer + backtest output ──────────────────────────────
models/*.bin
models/*.safetensors
models/*.pt
models/*.onnx

# ── Live file-state (journals, open positions) ───────────────────────────────
# Bot working state that must survive a redeploy. Adjust to your layout:
# ../fks-state/bots/crypto-futures/funding-paper.jsonl
# ../fks-state/bots/crypto-futures/funding-state-*.json
# ../fks-spawner/bots/spot-portfolio/spot-trades.jsonl

# ── Database tables — the runtime secret store + account/PnL state ───────────
# Dumped data-only (schema lives in src/sql/, applied at container init).
db:fks_db:exchange_secrets
db:janus_db:api_keys,api_key_audit
# Add account / position / pnl tables as your schema grows, e.g.:
# db:fks_db:bot_configs,bot_runs
# db:fks_db:accounts,transfers,net_worth_snapshots     (treasury layer)
# db:fks_db:edges,backtest_runs                        (edge factory)
